          "actualSpeechSec": 55.84362811791384,
          "segments": [
            {
              "index": 1,
              "text": "Today we're looking at a very common but fascinating process — evaporation. Let's start with the main idea.",
              "predictedSec": 7.3,
              "actualSec": 6.560907029478458,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/1/1fa78339c3cba13ffd3d4e829c5b09128e700b47d71fea3b6dd47b78f979c709.audio"
            },
            {
              "index": 2,
              "text": "Evaporation is the change of liquid water into water vapor. Notice it says this can happen right at the water surface — it doesn't need the water to boil. That's why puddles disappear even on a cool day.",
              "predictedSec": 12.6,
              "actualSec": 10.960907029478458,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/1/e6a727d10cca8c11e76c2580853737e266c97a6d24beb1bd940fe984aae0f862.audio"
            },
            {
              "index": 3,
              "text": "Now, point one — water vapor itself is invisible. You can't see it floating in the air. But we know it's there because of everyday evidence. Think about wet clothes hanging out to dry. After a while, they become dry. The liquid water didn't vanish — it turned into invisible vapor and moved into the air.",
              "predictedSec": 19.8,
              "actualSec": 18.560907029478457,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/1/19ca869e9d057aae48167c80d1c7dce0ca7662db84b42d7c84be18f1133da6e4.audio"
            },
            {
              "index": 4,
              "text": "Finally, if you want to test what affects drying speed — say, sun vs. shade — you must keep everything else the same. Use the same cloth, the same amount of water at the start. Only change the condition you're testing, then compare how long each takes to dry. That's a fair comparison, and it's the foundation of any good experiment.",
              "predictedSec": 20.7,
              "actualSec": 19.760907029478457,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/1/0aec6b4bbea5b4c5735e5985321e0236c94f817af16525f1c2834e4a2b5d58e9.audio"
            }
          ],
          "diagnosticOnly": true
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "targetSec": 50,
          "actualSpeechSec": 57.04272108843537,
          "segments": [
            {
              "index": 1,
              "text": "Let's talk about condensation — the process that changes water vapor back into liquid water. We just saw how evaporation turns liquid water into invisible vapor. Condensation is the reverse: vapor turning back into liquid.",
              "predictedSec": 14.6,
              "actualSec": 14.320907029478459,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/2/7ac1fe4ce9dddd94b3d7be36f523d32f5e8a7b5b37ecfd51b45af434daf66b1a.audio"
            },
            {
              "index": 2,
              "text": "Think about this: the air around us always contains water vapor. When that invisible vapor meets a surface that's cooler than the surrounding air, it loses energy and forms tiny liquid droplets. That's condensation happening right in front of you.",
              "predictedSec": 15.2,
              "actualSec": 14.400907029478459,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/2/7456df13b13ee62fff8d03853a9714cb14921ecdfd62308047c295308286d40d.audio"
            },
            {
              "index": 3,
              "text": "Here's a common question — have you ever noticed water droplets forming on the outside of a cold glass? Some people wonder if the water is seeping through the glass. But it's not. The glass is solid. What's really happening is water vapor from the warm air around the glass is condensing on the cold surface. The droplets come from the air, not from inside the glass. This example connects perfectly to what we discussed earlier: evaporation sends water into the air, and condensation brings it back down onto cool surfaces.",
              "predictedSec": 30.9,
              "actualSec": 28.32090702947846,
              "cached": false,
              "audioPath": "en-US/2/dc446139466074787ab738000b8cd68f6929fcc35fe4d0996506c2975de9fced.audio"
            }
          ],
          "diagnosticOnly": true
        }
